<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Enormous sums go unclaimed every year by people who qualify. Not through
    fraud in reverse or pride — mostly because nobody knew the thing existed,
    or assumed they earned too much, or looked at the form once and closed
    the tab.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is a screen for what your household might be entitled to, based on
    what the app already knows about your situation.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">How it works</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "It already knows most of it") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Household size, whether you rent or own, who you're caring for,
        what's happened to your work this year. So the screening is a short
        conversation rather than a form that asks your life story again.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "It surfaces the unlikely ones") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        The value isn't in the benefit everybody's heard of. It's in the
        credit for carers, or the thing that only applies in the year
        something changed — the ones people miss precisely because they've
        never heard of them.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "It ends in an action") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Not a list of possibilities. What to check, where to go, and the
        deadline on your calendar — because entitlements expire and that is
        how most of this money is lost.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "It watches for changes") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Eligibility follows life events: a birth, a job loss, becoming a
        carer, a move. When your circumstances change, it's worth asking the
        question again, and the app can notice that moment.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">A screen, not a determination</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    It tells you what looks worth investigating and why. It cannot tell you
    that you qualify — only the body running the scheme can do that, rules
    differ by where you live, and they change. A tool that stated confident
    eligibility would be inventing the most consequential thing on the page.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Why it's private, and why that matters</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    Screening for benefits means describing your household's money, health
    and difficulties in detail. Doing that on a website means telling a
    company all of it. Doing it here means telling your own computer, which
    is the difference between a screen you'll answer honestly and one you
    won't.
  </p>
</section>
